if (!exists("p_cooks", envir = .envir_result, inherits = FALSE)) {
  list(correct = FALSE, type = "warning", message = "Save the plot as `p_cooks`.")
} else if (!exists("cook_cut", envir = .envir_result, inherits = FALSE)) {
  list(correct = FALSE, type = "info", message = "Compute `cook_cut <- 4 / nobs(lm_model)`.")
} else if (!grepl("geom_text_repel|geom_hline", code)) {
  list(correct = FALSE, type = "info", message = "Add the dashed cutoff line and label influential points with `geom_text_repel()`.")
} else {
  cc <- get("cook_cut", envir = .envir_result)
  n_inf <- if (exists("influential", envir = .envir_result, inherits = FALSE)) {
    nrow(get("influential", envir = .envir_result))
  } else NA
  if (abs(cc - 4/151) < 0.001 && !is.na(n_inf) && n_inf >= 5) {
    list(correct = TRUE, type = "success", message = paste0(n_inf, " influential cases above 4/n — flagged, not removed."))
  } else {
    list(correct = TRUE, type = "success", message = "Cook's distance plot complete — check cases above the dashed line.")
  }
}
```
:::




::: {.callout-note appearance="simple"}
## Outliers vs influence

A point can be an outlier in Y without strongly influencing the slope. Cook's distance combines **leverage** and **residual size**. The 4/n cutoff is a **screening rule** — investigate flagged cases, but do not winsorize or trim without justification.
:::

